{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfnytxsr","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 2 Offline","year":2009,"examDate":2009,"subject":"physics","chapter":"waves","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"basic-of-waves-and-progressive-waves","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"punder-the-influence-of-the-coulomb-field-of-charge-q-a-jee-advanced-physics-motion-yxsneve7bukvjg3n","content":"<p>Under the influence of the Coulomb field of charge +Q, a charge <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>q is moving around it in an elliptical orbit. Find out the correct statement(s):</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"The angular momentum of the charge <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>q is constant."},{"identifier":"B","content":"The linear momentum of the charge <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http: